<!-- ============================================================
     ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875 Pre-Authentication RCE
     Glide Scripting Engine Sandbox Escape

     Threat:
       Pre-authentication remote code execution in the ServiceNow
       AI Platform Glide scripting engine sandbox (CVSS 9.5). An
       unauthenticated attacker sends a crafted request to
       /assessment_thanks.do to escape the Glide/Rhino JavaScript
       sandbox and execute arbitrary code in the context of the
       ServiceNow application server (Tomcat/JVM).

       ServiceNow Advisory: KB3137947
       Hosted instances: auto-patched early July 2026
       Self-hosted patch date: July 13, 2026
       CISA KEV: Added July 15, 2026

       Second bypass chain: Defused researchers confirmed active
       in-the-wild exploitation on July 19, 2026 and disclosed a
       second gadget chain that bypasses initial workarounds. Both
       chains target /assessment_thanks.do; rules here detect both
       based on the shared entry point and response behavior.

     Exploit anatomy:
       A crafted POST/PUT/PATCH to /assessment_thanks.do with a
       Glide script injection payload triggers the sandbox escape.
       Payload patterns may include Java reflection via Rhino
       (Packages.java.lang.Runtime, getRuntime().exec), GraalVM
       polyglot context abuse, or prototype chain pollution. No
       confirmed public PoC payload strings at time of authoring;
       detection anchors on method and response code.

     Post-exploitation indicators:
       Following successful RCE the attacker can spawn OS processes
       from the JVM context. Auditd execve records show shell and
       network tool invocations with the ServiceNow installation
       directory as cwd.

     MITRE ATT&amp;CK Techniques:
       T1190     - Exploit Public-Facing Application
       T1059     - Command and Scripting Interpreter
       T1071     - Application Layer Protocol (C2)
       T1041     - Exfiltration over C2 Channel

     Rule IDs: 104082-104088
     Author: SecOps Engineer (Purple Team)
     Issue: ESKA-593
     Date: 2026-07-21

     Log source prerequisites:
       Rules 104082-104086 (web detection):
         Traefik access log in JSON format forwarded to Wazuh.
         Required fields: RequestMethod, RequestPath, RequestHost,
         DownstreamStatus, ClientHost.
         Decoder: built-in Wazuh JSON decoder (decoded_as=json).
       Rules 104087-104088 (post-exploitation):
         Linux auditd with execve syscall auditing enabled.
         Wazuh must receive auditd events (auditd.log forwarded
         via localfile block or auditd plugin). ServiceNow cwd
         patterns cover common Linux installation paths:
           /opt/servicenow  /home/servicenow
           /srv/servicenow  /glide  /usr/share/glide
         Adjust the cwd pattern if your installation differs.

     Severity tiers:
       0  - Any request to /assessment_thanks.do (anchor only)
       14 - POST/PUT/PATCH to vulnerable endpoint (exploit attempt)
       15 - HTTP 2xx response to exploit request (RCE may be live)
       13 - 3+ requests from same source in 60 s (scanner)
       14 - Glide/Java sandbox escape payload patterns in request URI
       13 - Shell or recon binary from ServiceNow JVM cwd
       15 - Network or encoding tool from ServiceNow JVM cwd (C2/exfil)

     References:
       Help Net Security (2026-07-20): ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875
         Pre-Auth RCE Actively Exploited, Second Bypass Chain
       ServiceNow Advisory KB3137947:
         https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&amp;sysparm_article=KB3137947
       CISA KEV: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog
       NVD CVE-2026-6875:
         https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-6875
       MITRE ATT&amp;CK T1190:
         https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="initial_access,exploit_pubfacing,servicenow,cve_2026_6875,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104082: Base anchor - any request to /assessment_thanks.do
       Traefik access log (JSON decoder)
       Level 0: no alert; chains to rules 104083-104085.

       /assessment_thanks.do is the ServiceNow endpoint targeted
       by CVE-2026-6875. In normal operation this endpoint serves
       a static thank-you page to survey respondents via GET. No
       legitimate automated system sends POST, PUT, or PATCH to
       this path. Any access to this path from an external or
       unexpected source warrants investigation.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104082" level="0">
    <decoded_as>json</decoded_as>
    <field name="RequestPath" type="pcre2">(?i)/assessment_thanks\.do\b</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875: request to /assessment_thanks.do from $(ClientHost) (base anchor, chains to 104083-104085)</description>
    <group>servicenow,initial_access,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104083: POST/PUT/PATCH to /assessment_thanks.do
       Traefik access log (JSON decoder)
       MITRE: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)
       Child of rule 104082.

       /assessment_thanks.do only accepts GET in legitimate
       ServiceNow use. POST, PUT, and PATCH to this path are not
       part of any ServiceNow workflow and represent the primary
       exploit delivery mechanism for CVE-2026-6875. The Glide
       sandbox escape is triggered by a crafted request body or
       parameter injection delivered via these methods. This rule
       fires on both the original chain and the second bypass chain
       disclosed by Defused on July 19, 2026, since both target
       the same endpoint with mutating HTTP methods.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104083" level="14">
    <if_sid>104082</if_sid>
    <field name="RequestMethod" type="pcre2">^(?:POST|PUT|PATCH)$</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875: $(RequestMethod) to /assessment_thanks.do from $(ClientHost) to $(RequestHost)$(RequestPath) - active exploitation attempt; this endpoint serves only GET in normal operation; mutating HTTP methods trigger Glide scripting engine sandbox escape (CVSS 9.5 pre-auth RCE, CISA KEV July 15 2026); investigate source IP and correlate with response code (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,initial_access,exploit_pubfacing,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104084: HTTP 2xx response to exploit attempt
       Traefik access log (JSON decoder)
       MITRE: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)
       Child of rule 104083 (POST/PUT/PATCH to endpoint).

       A successful HTTP 2xx response to a mutating method on
       /assessment_thanks.do indicates the ServiceNow application
       processed the crafted request body. In the CVE-2026-6875
       exploitation chain the Glide sandbox evaluates the injected
       script before returning the response; a 2xx at this stage
       means arbitrary code may have executed in the JVM context.
       Level 15: immediate incident response required. Isolate the
       ServiceNow instance, preserve logs, and check for child
       process spawning and network connections from the JVM.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104084" level="15">
    <if_sid>104083</if_sid>
    <field name="DownstreamStatus" type="pcre2">^2\d{2}$</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875 CRITICAL: $(RequestMethod) to /assessment_thanks.do returned HTTP $(DownstreamStatus) to $(ClientHost) at $(RequestHost) - successful response to exploit request; Glide sandbox escape may be confirmed; arbitrary code may be executing in the JVM context; initiate immediate incident response: isolate instance, preserve logs, audit child processes and outbound connections (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,initial_access,exploit_pubfacing,rce_confirmed,critical,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104085: Automated scanner - 3+ requests in 60 seconds
       MITRE: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)

       Automated exploit frameworks and scanning tools probe
       /assessment_thanks.do with rapid repeated requests to
       fingerprint endpoint availability and iterate over payload
       variants for both the original and second bypass gadget
       chains. Three or more requests from the same source within
       60 seconds is a strong automated-tool signal. Recommend
       immediate firewall block on the source IP.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104085" level="13" frequency="3" timeframe="60">
    <if_matched_sid>104082</if_matched_sid>
    <same_field>ClientHost</same_field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875: 3+ requests to /assessment_thanks.do from $(ClientHost) within 60 s - automated exploit scanner or tool probing CVE-2026-6875 pre-auth RCE; $(RequestHost) is actively targeted; recommend blocking source IP at firewall (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,initial_access,exploit_pubfacing,scanner,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104086: Glide/Java sandbox escape payload in request URI
       Traefik access log (JSON decoder)
       MITRE: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)

       CVE-2026-6875 sandbox escape exploits Rhino (Mozilla JS
       engine embedded in the ServiceNow Glide scripting engine)
       or GraalVM polyglot context to reach the underlying JVM.
       Common gadget patterns visible in URI query strings include:
         Packages.java      - Rhino Java package namespace prefix
         java.lang.Runtime  - JVM process execution class
         getRuntime         - Runtime instance getter used in exec chain
         ProcessBuilder     - alternative JVM process execution class
         polyglot           - GraalVM polyglot context escape API
         __proto__          - prototype chain pollution patterns
       This rule fires on any ServiceNow path (not only
       assessment_thanks.do) to catch variant payloads that attempt
       to route through other .do endpoints after the second bypass
       chain was published. Correlate with rule 104082 to confirm
       the canonical CVE-2026-6875 target path.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104086" level="14">
    <decoded_as>json</decoded_as>
    <field name="RequestPath" type="pcre2">(?i)/[^"]+\.do[^"]*(?:Packages\.java|java\.lang\.(?:Runtime|ProcessBuilder|Thread|Class)|getRuntime|\.exec\(|polyglot\.eval|__proto__|constructor\[|java%2Elang|java%2flang)</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875: Glide or Java sandbox escape payload detected in request URI from $(ClientHost) to $(RequestHost)$(RequestPath) - Rhino/GraalVM gadget pattern in .do endpoint query string; consistent with CVE-2026-6875 first or second bypass chain exploitation; immediate investigation required (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,initial_access,exploit_pubfacing,payload_detected,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104087: Shell or recon binary from ServiceNow JVM cwd
       Log source: Linux auditd execve records
       MITRE: T1059 (Command and Scripting Interpreter)

       Following a successful CVE-2026-6875 sandbox escape the
       attacker executes OS commands through the compromised JVM
       process. Child processes inherit the ServiceNow installation
       directory as their working directory (cwd). Shell, scripting,
       and reconnaissance binaries executed with a ServiceNow cwd
       have no legitimate justification and confirm post-exploitation
       code execution. Covers common ServiceNow installation paths
       on Linux (/opt/servicenow, /glide, /srv/servicenow, etc.).
       Adjust the cwd pattern to match the actual installation path
       if your deployment uses a non-standard directory.
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104087" level="13">
    <decoded_as>auditd</decoded_as>
    <field name="full_log" type="pcre2">(?i)cwd=(?:/opt/servicenow|/home/servicenow|/srv/servicenow|/glide|/usr/share/glide|/var/servicenow)</field>
    <field name="audit.exe" type="pcre2">(?i)/(?:bash|sh|dash|ksh|csh|tcsh|zsh|python3?|perl|ruby|php|whoami|id|uname|hostname|cat|ls|find|ps|netstat|ss|ifconfig|ip|awk|sed|sort|cut)</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875: shell or recon binary $(audit.exe) executed from ServiceNow working directory on $(hostname) - post-exploitation command execution following Glide sandbox RCE; investigate JVM process ancestry and audit system for additional payloads dropped (T1059)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1059</id>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,post_exploitation,execution,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Rule 104088: Network or encoding tool from ServiceNow JVM cwd
       Log source: Linux auditd execve records
       MITRE: T1059, T1071, T1041

       Network tools (curl, wget, nc, ncat) and encoding utilities
       (base64, xxd) executed from the ServiceNow JVM working
       directory indicate active C2 channel establishment or
       payload staging following the initial RCE. These binaries
       have no legitimate operational role in the ServiceNow JVM
       process context. Level 15: immediate incident response
       required - the attacker is actively operating within the
       compromised ServiceNow host and may be staging lateral
       movement or exfiltrating ServiceNow ITSM data (service
       tickets, asset records, employee records, credentials).
       =========================================================== -->
  <rule id="104088" level="15">
    <decoded_as>auditd</decoded_as>
    <field name="full_log" type="pcre2">(?i)cwd=(?:/opt/servicenow|/home/servicenow|/srv/servicenow|/glide|/usr/share/glide|/var/servicenow)</field>
    <field name="audit.exe" type="pcre2">(?i)/(?:curl|wget|nc|ncat|nmap|masscan|socat|ssh|scp|sftp|rsync|base64|xxd|openssl|python3?|perl)</field>
    <description>ServiceNow CVE-2026-6875 CRITICAL: network or encoding tool $(audit.exe) executed from ServiceNow working directory on $(hostname) - active C2 establishment or data exfiltration following CVE-2026-6875 pre-auth RCE; ServiceNow contains high-value ITSM, HR, and asset data; initiate immediate incident response: isolate host, revoke all ServiceNow sessions, preserve auditd logs, and audit network connections from the JVM process (T1059/T1071/T1041)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1059</id>
      <id>T1071</id>
      <id>T1041</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>servicenow,post_exploitation,c2,exfiltration,critical,cve_2026_6875,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
